WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.449
The ablations clarify the design choices.

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:08.978
Increasing the number of discrete hue rotations
makes the network more robust to test-time hue shifts,

00:00:09.058 --> 00:00:13.507
though it slightly reduces capacity because
channels must shrink to keep parameters fixed.

00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:18.036
Group coset pooling turns out to be the mechanism
that yields hue invariance;

00:00:18.116 --> 00:00:22.565
remove it, and the network behaves like a regular one.

00:00:22.645 --> 00:00:27.094
Finally,

00:00:27.174 --> 00:00:31.623
color equivariance and color-jitter augmentation
are complementary: an equivariant network

00:00:31.703 --> 00:00:36.152
needs a lower intensity of augmentation to reach
the same robustness.

00:00:36.232 --> 00:00:40.681
A color-selectivity analysis further explains when
the method helps,

00:00:40.761 --> 00:00:45.210
showing that datasets with more color-selective
neurons benefit from equivariance up to later stages.
